\f1\fs22 The High Elvis met Chanta on the road, in view of the circle of Agent Jones clones cordoning off the hover-pad. Across the road, if the shuttle buses weren\'92t exactly dancing in time to the music, they seemed to be rocking on their suspension more than they were an hour earlier.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 \'93What news of your walk?\'94 The High Elvis asked.\
\'93Someone needs to drop the gates. People need to get home for Christmas.\'94\
\'93That would be under Ms Shakti\'92s control,\'94 the High Elvis said. \'93Did you meet with the Holy Momma?\'94\
\'93You know I didn\'92t.\'94 Chanta looked back across to the office park where the 
\fs20 TRAVERSE STATION
\fs22  sign glowed. \'93Your hound dogs didn\'92t follow me down.\'94\
\'93We know what is there.\'94\
\'93I heard the tone in Sarah\'92s voice. She was hiding something.\'94 Chanta couldn\'92t believe she was just hiding out in a bunker, playing happy families with Alexander and Eloise. Something else was going on. \'93We have to rescue her.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \'93
\f1\fs22 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth0 The Holy Momma needs no rescuing. We will attend her at the right time, when the birth of the One after the One is imminent.\'94\
\'93I want to attend her now.\'94\
\'93It is not yet the time. Allow the Holy Momma her rest, Wise Humper.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'93Please don\'92t call me that.\'94 \
The High Elvis took half a step to the side. \'93Apologies. Thank you for the correction, Great Humper.\'94\
Chanta looked the High Elvis over. \'93Do you have a problem with me?\'94\
\'93I\'92m sorry?\'94\
\'93I\'92m the Great Teacher. You would all still be squabbling over lyrics if it weren\'92t for me.\'94\
\'93Perhaps,\'94 the High Elvis answered. \'93Or perhaps we just needed something to shift us past the squabbling. It could have been anything, timed and deployed well. That, I think, is my predecessor's greatest contribution.\'94\
Chanta\'92s face hardened. \'93Well, I\'92m going to rescue Sarah, with or without your help.\'94\
\'93The Holy Momma needs no rescuing,\'94 the High Elvis repeated, which only got Chanta\'92s back up. \'93You saw it yourself,\'94 the High Elvis continued. \'93There is too much activity at the station right now.\'94\
\'93You could stop the music.\'94\
\'93That would make it worse.\'94\
Chanta suspected the High Elvis was right. \'93I don\'92t want anyone hurt.\'94\
The High Elvis put his hand on Chanta\'92s shoulder. \'93Then give it an hour, maybe two, for use of the Traverse to settle down.\'94\
Chanta chewed his mouth around while he thought. \'94I dunno. I thought we could take control of the station, stop people going down there.\'94\
\'93So the Great Humper speaks of taking control now?\'94\
\'93Hey, you're twisting my words.\'94 Chanta wasn\'92t sure whether the High Elvis was scolding him for now, or for not taking control months ago. When he had the chance.\
\'93You speak of twisting words,\'94 the High Elvis said. \'93You tried to twist ours. 
\f3\i We won't praise the Dawkins
\f1\i0 ? You thought that would work? In any case, there are too many innocent people up and about. Give it an hour.\'94\
Chanta gave it an hour, while he retired to the state room of his hover-copt and was received by the Elvisettes, who eased his bubbled mind, and rocked him, rolled him, and drained him of the sap of his wakefulness.
